    <li>To solve this problem, we will use the same method we did for problem 6. With the values given we can plug them into the formula to obtain (0.9572&nbsp;&times; 31.9720) + (0.0051&nbsp;&times; 32.9715) + (0.0422&nbsp;&times; 33.9679) = 32.2052amu. The periodic table states that the mass of sulfur is 32.06amu, meaning that the measurements are not entirely accurate.</li>
